.TH ZERODDS-MQTT-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-mqtt-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-mqtt-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the MQTT bridge daemon maps DDS topics onto MQTT
topics. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-mqtt-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the parser that reads it is
.IR crates/mqtt-bridge/src/daemon/config.rs::load_from_str .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " mqtt ", " auth ", " acl ", " metrics ", " topics ", " tenants .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr and starts with the
defaults \(em watch the WARN log.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed, so
credentials belong in the environment, not in the file.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS mqtt
.TP
.B broker_url
.IR mqtt:// ", " mqtts:// ", " ws:// " or " wss://
URL of the broker, e.g.
.IR "mqtt://localhost:1883"
or
.IR "wss://broker:443/mqtt" .
The WebSocket schemes carry MQTT in binary frames (MQTT 5.0 \(sc6); the path
defaults to
.IR /mqtt .
.TP
.B client_id
MQTT client identifier; must be unique on the broker. Default
.IR zerodds-bridge-<host> ,
the host name of the operating system.
.TP
.B protocol_version
.IR 5 " (default) or " 3.1.1 .
Under 3.1.1 the daemon is an MQTT 3.1.1 client: no properties in CONNECT
and PUBLISH (spec \(sc1 L1); a DDS dispose or unregister is then not
published, it is logged and counted as an error (spec \(sc4.4).
.TP
.B drain_timeout_secs
Seconds the shutdown waits for the broker's acknowledgements of QoS 1/2
messages before DISCONNECT (spec \(sc9.2). Default 30; a value too large
for the clock of the system waits without end.
.TP
.B keep_alive_secs
CONNECT keep-alive in seconds. The daemon sends PINGREQ when it has sent
nothing for that long and closes the connection when the PINGRESP does not
come within half of it; the broker's Server Keep Alive replaces the value.
.I 0
switches it off.
.TP
.B clean_start
Boolean.
.I false
keeps the session across a reconnect and a restart of the daemon, with a
.B session_expiry_interval_secs
above 0 (under 3.1.1 always); the client side of it is kept in
.BR session_dir .
.I true
discards it.
.TP
.B session_expiry_interval_secs
Session Expiry Interval of the CONNECT. Default
.IR 0 :
the session ends with the connection.
.TP
.B session_dir
Directory of the client's Session State of a session that outlives its
connection: the QoS 1/2 messages the broker has not acknowledged and the
broker's QoS 2 messages not yet released, one file
.I <client id>.session
and its lock file per connection, written before each packet. After a
restart, a CONNACK with Session Present 1 resends them (spec \(sc4.1).
It also holds the replay buffer
.I <client id>.replay
of the persistent topics (spec \(sc6).
Default
.I /var/lib/zerodds/mqtt-bridge
.RI ( /usr/local/var/lib/zerodds/mqtt-bridge
on macOS). A directory the daemon cannot create or write, or a file another
process holds, prevents the start (exit 1).
.TP
.B max_packet_size
Maximum Packet Size of the CONNECT, 1 to 16777216 octets (the default). A
larger packet of the broker ends the connection with DISCONNECT 0x95.
.TP
.B receive_maximum
Receive Maximum of the CONNECT, 1 to 65535 (the default): QoS 2 messages
of the broker held unreleased at once; more end the connection with 0x93.
.TP
.B topic_alias_maximum
Topic Alias Maximum of the CONNECT, 0 to 65535, default
.IR 100 .
.TP
.B connect_timeout_secs
How long the start tries a broker it cannot reach before exit 2: a wait of
.B reconnect
that would pass it is shortened to it and the last attempt starts there.
An attempt waits at most 10 s for the TCP connection and 5 s for each
answer of the broker. Default
.IR 30 ;
.I 0
tries without end, and so does a value too large for the clock of the
system.
.TP
.B reconnect
Sub-map: the waits between two connect attempts.
.B initial_delay_ms
(default 500, at least 1) after the first,
.B factor
(default 2.0, at least 1.0) times the last for each further one, at most
.B max_delay_ms
(default 30000).
.TP
.B own_topic_prefix
The topic levels in front of
.I <client_id>/
in the daemon's own topics: the retained catalog
.RI ( <prefix>/<client_id>/catalog ,
spec \(sc5.2), the reports of a missed deadline and a lost liveliness and
the will of the CONNECT
.RI ( <prefix>/<client_id>/liveliness_lost ,
spec \(sc6). Default
.IR $zerodds .
MQTT 5.0 \(sc4.7.2 leaves the topics beginning with
.I $
to the broker: HiveMQ 4 refuses a will there with CONNACK 0x82 and ends the
connection of a PUBLISH there, so it needs a prefix such as
.IR zerodds .
Not empty, no
.IR + ", " #
and no trailing
.IR / .
A change needs a restart.
.TP
.B username ", " password
Legacy credentials for the CONNECT packet. They are a fallback:
.BR auth.username " and " auth.password
win when both are set.
.TP
.B tls
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean),
.B ca_file
(trust anchor for the broker certificate),
.BR cert_file " and " key_file
(client material for mTLS, set together; material that does not load
ends the start with exit 4),
.B server_name
(SNI/hostname override),
.B verify_hostname
(only
.IR true ;
.I false
prevents the start, the certificate is always checked against the name)
and
.B alpn
(list of the protocol names the TLS handshake offers; default
.I mqtt
under
.IR mqtts:// ,
.I http/1.1
under
.IR wss:// ).
The client keys are named
.BR cert_file / key_file ,
not
.IR client_cert_file / client_key_file .
A
.I mqtts://
or
.I wss://
URL needs
.B enabled
true, a
.I mqtt://
or
.I ws://
URL refuses it.
.SS auth
How the daemon authenticates towards the broker (\(sc7.2).
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " password " | " mtls " | " enhanced ;
.IR bearer ", " sasl " and " sasl_plain
are other names of
.IR password .
Not set:
.I enhanced
with
.BR enhanced ,
.I password
with a user name, a password or
.BR bearer_token ,
.I mtls
with
.B mqtt.tls.cert_file
under
.BR mqtt.tls.enabled ,
else
.IR none .
.I none
connects anonymously and only to a broker on the loopback interface
.RI ( localhost ", 127.0.0.0/8, " ::1 ).
.I password
sends User Name and Password.
.I mtls
presents the client certificate and sends neither.
.I enhanced
is MQTT 5.0 enhanced authentication. Settings that do not fit the mode
prevent the start (exit 1).
.TP
.B username ", " password
User name and password of
.I password
and of SCRAM-SHA-256; they win over
.B mqtt.username
and
.BR mqtt.password .
.TP
.B bearer_token
The token: the CONNECT password under
.I password
(not together with
.BR auth.password ),
the OAUTHBEARER token or the Authentication Data of another method under
.IR enhanced .
.TP
.B bearer_subject
The daemon's subject for the ACL in place of the one it has (see
.BR acl ).
.TP
.B enhanced
Map with
.BR method ,
the Authentication Method under
.IR enhanced :
.I SCRAM-SHA-256
(RFC 7677; the broker's signature is checked, a failure is exit 5),
.I OAUTHBEARER
(RFC 7628), or another method that takes
.B bearer_token
as one message. Needs
.B mqtt.protocol_version
5. A reload with new credentials re-authenticates the standing connection
(AUTH 0x19); a reload that keeps them sends none.
.SS acl
Daemon-side access control, evaluated before MQTT. The subject is the
daemon's own identity towards the broker: the DN of the client certificate
in
.B mqtt.tls.cert_file
(RFC 4514, or its fingerprint
.IR mtls: <sha256>),
else the user name it authenticates with, else the
.I sub
claim of the JWT in
.BR auth.bearer_token ;
.B auth.bearer_subject
replaces it. The daemon's own topics under
.I <prefix>/<client_id>/
.RI ( <prefix>
is
.BR mqtt.own_topic_prefix )
are not subject to the ACL.
.TP
.B default_deny
Boolean. Decides the topics no rule names:
.I true
refuses them,
.I false
allows them. Not set:
.I true
once a rule exists,
.I false
without rules.
.TP
.B rules
List of rules. Each entry carries
.B subject
.RI ( * :
every subject) and the lists of MQTT topic filters
.B allow_publish
(the PUBLISH packets the daemon sends) and
.B allow_subscribe
(the subscriptions within a filter, and the PUBLISH packets the broker
delivers). A topic that only rules of other subjects name is refused. A
refusal is logged as
.I acl_denied
and counted in
.IR zerodds_mqtt_bridge_acl_denials_total .
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9092"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
The key is
.BR listen ,
not
.IR address .
.TP
.B path
The path of the Prometheus metrics on the admin endpoint. Default
.IR /metrics ;
not
.IR / ", " /catalog " or " /healthz .
The families (\(sc8.2), each with the prefix
.IR zerodds_mqtt_bridge_ :
.IR connect_attempts_total ,
.IR connect_successes_total ,
.IR publish_in_total {dds_topic,mqtt_qos},
.IR publish_out_total {dds_topic,mqtt_qos},
.IR bytes_in_total {dds_topic},
.IR bytes_out_total {dds_topic},
.IR inflight_messages {direction},
.IR dds_samples_received_total {dds_topic},
.IR dds_samples_published_total {dds_topic},
.IR acl_denials_total {reason},
.IR broker_disconnects_total {reason_code},
.IR dds_samples_dropped_total {dds_topic},
.IR errors_total .
.SS topics (list)
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B dds_type
Fully-qualified IDL type.
.TP
.B mqtt_topic
MQTT topic or filter. Defaults to a slug of
.BR dds_name .
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries MQTT messages from the broker into DDS (the daemon subscribes on
the broker and creates a DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to the broker (a DataReader, published to
.BR mqtt_topic ),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
.TP
.B mqtt_qos
.IR 0 " | " 1 " | " 2 .
Not set: 1 for a reliable topic, 0 for a best-effort one.
.TP
.B retain
Boolean; sets the MQTT retain flag on published messages. Not set: true for
the durabilities
.IR transient_local ", " transient " and " persistent .
.TP
.B data_representation
.IR xcdr1 " | " xcdr2 :
the one data representation the topic's DataWriter offers from its creation
and its DataReader accepts (DDS-XTypes 1.3 \(sc7.6.3.1). A DDS reader of
another vendor that accepts only XCDR2 matches the DataWriter before the
first PUBLISH only with
.IR xcdr2 .
A DDS writer that offers only the other representation matches no
DataReader of the topic
.RI ( out ", " bidir ):
its samples do not reach MQTT.
A PUBLISH whose encapsulation header names the other XCDR version is
refused: logged as
.IR publish_refused ,
counted as an error, not written. Not set: the DataWriter offers XCDR1 and
takes the representation of the header of each PUBLISH, the DataReader
accepts both (spec \(sc3, \(sc4.2).
.TP
.B schema_url
Optional; where the schema of the topic's type is published. The retained
catalog on
.I <prefix>/<client_id>/catalog
.RI ( <prefix>
is
.BR mqtt.own_topic_prefix )
and
.I /catalog
of the admin endpoint carry it (spec \(sc5.2).
.TP
.B qos
DDS QoS sub-map with
.BR reliability ", " durability " and "
.B history
carrying
.B kind
.RI ( keep_last ", the default, or " keep_all )
and
.B depth
(default 10): the HISTORY of the topic's DataWriter
.RI ( in ", " bidir )
and the samples the daemon holds while the broker acknowledges nothing
.RI ( out ", " bidir ):
.I keep_last
the newest
.B depth
of each instance (the older ones are dropped and counted),
.I keep_all
every one (spec \(sc6). Further keys of
.BR qos :
.B lifespan_ms
(the LIFESPAN of the DataWriter and the Message Expiry Interval of a sample
whose writer names none, less the time the sample waited in the daemon; a
sample whose lifespan passed while it waited is not published and is
counted as dropped),
.B deadline_ms
(the DEADLINE of both endpoints; a missed one is a retained message on
.IR <prefix>/<client_id>/deadline_missed/<slug> ,
.I <prefix>
being
.BR mqtt.own_topic_prefix ),
.B liveliness
with
.B kind
.RI ( automatic ", " manual_by_participant ", " manual_by_topic )
and
.B lease_ms
(a DDS writer that loses it is a message on
.IR <prefix>/<client_id>/liveliness_lost/<slug> ),
.B partition
(the DDS partitions of both endpoints; the samples of another partition are
not published). Not set: infinite, AUTOMATIC, the default partition; a
.BR lifespan_ms ,
.B deadline_ms
or
.B lease_ms
of 2147483647000 or more (2^31 \- 1 s) is infinite as well. A
topic with durability
.I transient
or
.I persistent
keeps the newest sample of each instance and publishes them again after
each CONNACK;
.I persistent
also in
.I <client id>.replay
in
.B session_dir
(spec \(sc6).
.SS tenants (list)
Participants and broker connections beside those of
.B domain
(spec \(sc1 L6). Each entry carries
.B name
(unique, without
.IR / ),
.B domain
(default: the top-level one),
.B mqtt
with
.B client_id
(required; the tenant's binding on the broker, not the one of the top level
or of another tenant),
.B username
and
.B password
(default: the top level's credentials; in the mode of the top level they
replace the user name and password of
.I password
and of SCRAM-SHA-256, and where the top level presents
.BR auth.bearer_token ,
the password is the tenant's token; a user name or password the mode does
not use, such as a user name under
.IR OAUTHBEARER ,
prevents the start, exit 1),
.B topics
(as above) and
.B acl
(as above, for the tenant's topics).
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/mqtt-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged (1),
.BR zerodds-xmlc (1).
